  "id": "BIT-nginx-gateway-fabric-2026-125283",
  "summary": "NGINX try_files vulnerability",
  "details": "When NGINX Plus or NGINX Open Source is configured to use the try_files and alias directives with a map variable, certain combinations of regular expression captures in map and try_files can cause a segmentation fault in an NGINX worker process.\n\nImpact:\nAn attacker could leverage this vulnerability to cause an NGINX worker process to terminate unexpectedly. There is no control plane exposure; this is a data plane issue only.\n\n\n\nNote: Software versions which have reached End of Technical Support (EoTS) are not evaluated.",
